timeshift-tray (1.0.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Fix a crash and a file-descriptor leak when the snapshot location goes away
  * Fix a read loop that could stop for good, freezing the tray silently
  * Fix a connection leak that could exhaust file descriptors in a day
  * Work on GLib 2.46 and later again, instead of dying on first export
  * Rate-limit the snapshot wrapper; harden both wrappers; add revoke-access
  * Redraw the icons so the five states differ at 16px and recolour on Plasma
  * Extract controller.py and add 38 tests for the orderings behind these fixes

 -- makeafide <willsmit4433@gmail.com>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:57:23 -0400

timeshift-tray (1.0.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: a StatusNotifierItem tray applet showing the last
    snapshot, the scheduler's state and the snapshot location, with live
    progress for any job the daemon is running -- including ones started by
    apt-snapshot-guard rather than by the user
  * "Create snapshot now" runs a fixed-argument wrapper through pkexec, under
    a policy action that authorises that one command and not the Timeshift CLI
  * Runs as the desktop user over the daemon's read-only interface, and
    explains how to get access rather than failing silently when the user is
    not in the timeshift group

 -- makeafide <willsmit4433@gmail.com>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 09:07:09 -0400
